  "info": {
    "description": "Explicit proxy to Routeware WebRW. Session cookies are stored in a Worker Durable Object; clients do not send Routeware credentials.

**Customer:** \`customers-read\` lists rows; \`detail-full\` loads one record; \`customer-types-read\` feeds dropdowns; \`add-new-long\` and \`load-long-modal\` return the same HTML/JS shells the SPA uses before save; \`save-long-form\` creates or updates (URL-encoded form body). **Anti-forgery** for \`save-long-form\` is filled server-side from Routeware modal HTML when the client omits \`__RequestVerificationToken\` (see \`CUSTOMER_SAVE_AUTO_TOKEN\`). Routeware does not support HTTP DELETE for customers — use \`save-long-form\` with \`Enabled=false\` to disable. \`DELETE /api/v1/routeware/customer\` documents that limitation (returns 405 + problem+json).

**D1 snapshots (Routeware custom CSV reports):** \`customer_snapshot\` (CustomerID) → \`address_snapshot\` (PickupAddressID, CustomerID) → \`container_snapshot\` (ContainerID, PickupAddressID). **Export source:** set \`*_REPORT_EXPORT_PATH\` (static URL) **or** \`*_REPORT_QUERY_ID\` (WebRW: client \`requestID\` + \`GET\` \`QueryExecuteDownload\`), then \`POST /api/v1/data-snapshot/sync\` (bearer) or the daily cron. \`POST /api/v1/...-snapshot/import\` accepts a raw CSV body. See \`CUSTOMER_SNAPSHOT.md\` for setup and migration commands.

**Data entity (\`/api/v1/data/*\`, tag \`data-entity\`):** bearer = \`CUSTOMER_SNAPSHOT_SYNC_SECRET\`. \`GET\` reads nested D1 snapshots (customer + address + container graph) with ETag/cache. \`POST\` applies changes to Routeware, returns ids + sync outcome only (never submitted fields or the upstream body), then refreshes D1 from \`GetCustomerDetailFull\` and invalidates that cache for affected ids.",
    "title": "Routeware Shadow API",
    "version": "1.0.0",
  },
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "paths": {
    "/api/v1/address-snapshot": {
      "get": {
        "description": "Routeware addresses (\`PickupAddressID\` → \`CustomerID\`). Optional filters: \`customerId\`, \`pickupAddressId\`, free-text on street \`q\`, \`enabled\`. Pass \`cursor\` (the previous page's \`nextCursor\`) instead of \`offset\` to page deep result sets by primary-key seek instead of a scanned OFFSET.",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "customerId",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null",
              ],
            },
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "pickupAddressId",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null",
              ],
            },
          },
          {
            "description": "Address line substring (case-insensitive)",
            "in": "query",
            "name": "q",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "description": "Address line substring (case-insensitive)",
              "type": "string",
            },
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "enabled",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "default": "any",
              "enum": [
                "true",
                "false",
                "any",
              ],
              "type": "string",
            },
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "limit",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "default": 50,
              "maximum": 500,
              "minimum": 1,
              "type": "integer",
            },
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "offset",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "default": 0,
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null",
              ],
            },
          },
          {
            "description": "Last pickup_address_id from the previous page's nextCursor; takes precedence over offset",
            "in": "query",
            "name": "cursor",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "description": "Last pickup_address_id from the previous page's nextCursor; takes precedence over offset",
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null",
              ],
            },
          },
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CustomerSnapshotList",
                },
              },
            },
            "description": "Rows and total",
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Invalid query (application/problem+json). The zod validator rejects an out-of-range \`limit\`/\`offset\` or an unknown \`enabled\` value before any D1 query runs.",
          },
        },
        "summary": "List address snapshot rows (D1)",
        "tags": [
          "address-snapshot",
        ],
      },
    },
    "/api/v1/address-snapshot/export": {
      "get": {
        "description": "Streams every \`address_snapshot\` row as CSV (\`Content-Disposition: attachment\`, filename \`address-snapshot.csv\`) in \`pickup_address_id\` order. Reads in keyset pages so a full-table export never buffers the table in memory. Emits a content-hash \`ETag\`; replay it as \`If-None-Match\` for a \`304\` with an empty body. Requires \`Authorization: Bearer <CUSTOMER_SNAPSHOT_SYNC_SECRET>\`.",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "text/csv": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                },
              },
            },
            "description": "CSV download (header line plus one line per row)",
          },
          "304": {
            "description": "Not modified (If-None-Match carries the current ETag)",
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthorized",
          },
        },
        "summary": "Download address snapshot as CSV",
        "tags": [
          "address-snapshot",
        ],
      },
    },
    "/api/v1/address-snapshot/import": {
      "post": {
        "description": "Raw CSV (Routeware Address Details custom report). Bear same secret; import **customers** first to satisfy \`customer_id\` foreign keys.",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "text/csv": {
              "example": "PickupAddressID,CustomerID,RouteID,Address,City,State,Zip,FranchiseID,Comments,ExtrasAllowed,Enabled,DriverNote,Latitude,Longitude,Last_Audit_Date
10,5,,1 Main St,Killeen,TX,76541,,,false,true,,,,",
              "schema": {
                "type": "string",
              },
            },
          },
          "description": "Routeware Address Details CSV (header + data rows — see example)",
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "properties": {
                    "deleted": {
                      "type": "integer",
                    },
                    "rowCount": {
                      "type": "integer",
                    },
                    "upserted": {
                      "type": "integer",
                    },
                  },
                  "required": [
                    "upserted",
                    "rowCount",
                  ],
                  "type": "object",
                },
              },
            },
            "description": "Result",
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Empty body (application/problem+json). Returned when the POST has no request body; post the CSV as raw body.",
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthorized",
          },
        },
        "summary": "Import address CSV body into D1",
        "tags": [
          "address-snapshot",
        ],
      },
    },
    "/api/v1/address-snapshot/sync": {
      "post": {
        "description": "Same bearer as \`customer-snapshot\` sync. Requires \`ADDRESS_REPORT_EXPORT_PATH\` or \`ADDRESS_REPORT_QUERY_ID\`. Customers should exist in D1 (run customer import/sync first) so \`customer_id\` foreign keys are satisfied.",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "properties": {
                    "deleted": {
